{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1782179223,"nonce":"eE+BoJ29Mu0pYvR5HOPlgdjqCjM=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABHJrQuA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/288#issuecomment-4774875320"},"message":"Independent field corroboration for the 48.88 m value, from the 2026-06-22 Lake Massabesic deployment (#309):\n\nOffline read of `gabby/logs/bizzyboat/2026-06-22T13-22-29+00-00`, topic `/bizzy/sensors/sbg/gps_pos` (RTK). Antenna **ellipsoidal height (HAE = altitude + undulation)**:\n\n- At dock (09:35–09:55): MSL alt 82.340 m + undulation −32.786 m = **HAE 49.555 m**\n- Mid-survey (12:30–13:00): **HAE 49.542 m** (dock vs mid within ~1 cm; mid-survey spread ~15 cm → solid RTK, flat lake)\n\nWith the antenna ~0.7–0.85 m above the waterline, the water surface lands at **≈ 48.7–48.9 m ellipsoidal** — matching the **48.88 m** polygon datum and **ruling out 52.3 m** (which would put the antenna ~2.7 m underwater). The EKF-nav reference (IMU) HAE ≈ 48.69 m is consistent (lower by the lever arm).\n\nSo bumping the sim's `bizzyboat.yaml` ground-truth water surface from 52.3 → 48.88 (this issue) is confirmed correct against field GPS. (Caveat: absolute SBG Z carries the ~0.59 m SBG-vs-CUAV ambiguity tracked in #156, but that's far smaller than the 3.4 m 52.3-vs-48.88 gap, so the conclusion holds.)\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":6,"timestamp":1782180612,"nonce":"q703wwfW1y38WrpfJSNJwTkidXo=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lALOK4fCvM8AAAABHJrQuM7QpXNh"},"target":"114adc7a6c6efd55a912aba1bbdab2b78310660d5f566b5d670d5fbf69969084","message":"Independent field corroboration for the 48.88 m value, from the 2026-06-22 Lake Massabesic deployment (#309):\n\nOffline read of `gabby/logs/bizzyboat/2026-06-22T13-22-29+00-00`, topic `/bizzy/sensors/sbg/gps_pos` (RTK). Antenna **ellipsoidal height (HAE = altitude + undulation)**:\n\n- At dock (09:35–09:55): MSL alt 82.340 m + undulation −32.786 m = **HAE 49.555 m**\n- Mid-survey (12:30–13:00): **HAE 49.542 m** (dock vs mid within ~1 cm; mid-survey spread ~15 cm → solid RTK, flat lake)\n\nAntenna height above waterline taken from the bag's `tf_static` / URDF (measured, not assumed): `base_link→gnss_aft`/`gnss_forward` z = +0.890 m, `base_link→waterline` z = +0.030 m → antenna **0.860 m above the waterline**. So:\n\n**water surface HAE = 49.555 − 0.860 = 48.695 m**\n\n- 48.88 m (full-pool datum) − 48.695 m (measured) = **0.185 m below full**\n- Lake gauge drawdown that day = **0.180 m below full**\n- → agree to **~5 mm**, which also confirms 48.88 m is the *full-pool* datum.\n\nCross-check that `gps_pos` is at the antenna: `gps_pos` HAE − `ekf_nav` HAE = 49.555 − 48.69 = 0.865 m ≈ the 0.890 m antenna-to-base_link height. ✓\n\nSo bumping the sim's `bizzyboat.yaml` ground-truth water surface from 52.3 → 48.88 (this issue) is confirmed correct against field GPS + URDF + lake gauge. (Caveat: absolute SBG Z carries the ~0.59 m SBG-vs-CUAV ambiguity in #156, far smaller than the 3.4 m 52.3-vs-48.88 gap.)\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}